('Bayesian framing','We clarify that only BLR and GPC are Bayesian, while RF and L2 logistic regression are benchmarks. The title and abstract now reflect the comparative scope, and GPC inference is described as approximate and conditional on optimized hyperparameters.','Title; Abstract; Sections 1 and 3.1'),
('Rainfall triggering data','We explicitly limit the analysis to static susceptibility, add regional rainfall-threshold context and explain that missing event metadata prevents fitting or validating triggering thresholds. The CHIRPS aggregation period is not recoverable and is not invented.','Sections 2.3 and 5'),
